            <font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#333333">Thursday, 
            May&nbsp; 27&nbsp; 2004&nbsp;&nbsp;<font size=1><i>- posted by&nbsp;Conqueso</i></font><br>
            </font> 
            <hr>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td valign="top"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="4" color="#333333">A Special Update</font></td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" color="#333333" size="2">
            <table border="0" width="700">
<tr>
<td>
<font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#333333">

<p>We have a special update to make. It will be up for a limited time. We have recently elected Gravelbeard as our new guild leader. We all want to thank Veer for his hard work and dedication to the guild since May of 2003. He helped MoKB through the guild rebuild of last year. He saw us take on RZ and then saw us through the problems that happened in April. It takes a special person to fill the role of guild leader and is the reason why it took so long to start finding a replacement. Again, thank you Veer for wearing the mantle and being steadfast in your dedication through some very difficult times for the guild.
<p>
We quickly found out that Gravelbeard leads double lives. During the day, he is a battle-hardened dwarf. At night, he transforms into a disco demon. We were all surprised by dual lives that Gravelbeard lives. At first we did not believe it. Once again, we hired people to find out the true story and our fears were quickly confirmed. For a limited time, we shine a spotlight on the two lives of our new guildleader. However, the story does not end there. We also acquired footage of Gravelbeard performing his inaugural speech for the guild.
<p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>

<tr>
<td>
<table border="1" width="700" cellpadding="10" bordercolor="#000000">
<tr><td align="center">
<img src="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/SS/SS1576.jpg"><br />
