            <font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#333333">Wednesday, 
            March&nbsp; 10&nbsp; 2004&nbsp;&nbsp;<font size=1><i>- posted by&nbsp;Conqueso</i></font><br>
            </font> 
            <hr>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td valign="top"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="4" color="#333333">What's Up Doc?</font></td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td valign="top"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" color="#333333" size="2">
            <table border="0" width="700">
<tr>
<td>
<font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#333333">
<p>During the month of January, MoKB conducted over 31 raids. We thought it was time to take a nice vacation for the month of February. Some people caught up on sleep. A few people took trips to exotic places. We even had one person take time off for the army in Australia. Those boom-a-rangs are lethal. As with EQ and anything you do, knowing when to work hard and when to relax is essential. Here is some good advice to follow:

<p><i><center>"Don't take life too seriously. You'll never get out alive. - Bugs Bunny."
</i></center></font>
<br>
<tr><td align="center">
<font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#333333">
<img src="http://www.mokb.org/cgi-bin/SS/SS1529.jpg"><br />
<font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="-2" color="#3333FF">
Vacation Pictures</font></center><br />
<tr>
<td>
<font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2" color="#333333">
<p>We raided some during February but took things at an easy pace. We did about half the amount compared to January. Everyone is back now so we are now cranking things up again. Along with a few other places, we paid Xuzl and Arlyxir in Sol Ro a visit. Xuzl was a bit shy for the photographer. Unlike the cartoons, we won't end this with a "That's all folks," or "I should have taken that left turn at Albuquerque."
<p>
<p>
</font>
</td>
</tr>
